---
 
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Exciting_1>>

 
<<SetBGSprite hutInterior>>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Excited">>
Ramu: Captain.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Reporting.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Excited">>
Ramu: Today's not like the lane matches—there's a pot at the end with real notes, half for ground repairs, the rest for winners.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Anxious">>
Raju: Maa's medicines, Baba's knee towel, new soles for my shoes… I counted it twice in my head.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Confident">>
Ramu: Good. Count your breath the same way—twice before anything important, and remember: prize money is a reason, not a target.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Eyes, feet, hands, timing, temper—five coins in the pocket.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Exactly. You're the youngest here, and some will test you—let them, because people laugh before they clap.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: If they bowl words at me, I'll leave those outside off.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Leave well, and if older boys glare when you speak, lower your voice and raise your game—pride is loud, respect is heard.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I'll be a good teammate first, a good anything else after.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: That's the order. The captain will watch how you walk before he watches how you play—head up, shoulders easy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Raju reporting.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: For us. Stakes twist the wind, but when it pushes, don't push back—lean with it, then choose your moment.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: The bat is lighter now.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: That's you getting stronger. I retaped the toe last night—brick-sanded, face up when it rests?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Always.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Today is also about seeing—not just balls, but how the ground breathes, little truths about every player.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Like Parle-G crumbs—small but sweet.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Maa said, "Play brave and come back hungry." Whether you miss or shine, you breathe—and if someone else shines, you clap like it's your own sun.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Worried">>
Raju: Bhai, if we win, can we fix the tarp before the rain?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: First we fix our hearts before the toss, tarp will follow.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: I'm not asking you to be special, just steady—special happens to steady boys when the world is looking elsewhere.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Steady is my job.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Right. When pressure knocks, open the door and say, "Sit, watch me work."

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Thank you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Thank me by showing up like you did at dawn for fourteen months—make them see a teammate, not a kid.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: If someone asks how old I am?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Say, "Old enough to keep my promises."

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: You'll wait near the scorers' table, face up, chin up—and we don't let poverty steal our manners.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: We don't.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Whatever happens, we walk out and we walk back the same way—heads steady. If we carry anything extra, it's gratitude.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Go on, Captain. Make the ground remember you without making a noise about it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Reporting.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
<<FadeToBlack>>
<<StopBackgroundMusic>>
